.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "perturbation_channel_coregulation" "perturbation_channel_coregulation"
.SH NAME
perturbation_channel_coregulation \- Get or set the co-regulation fallback of the perturbation channel.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIperturbation_channel_coregulation(\fBgps\fR as <generic> GPSModel, 
\fBenabled\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get or set the co-regulation fallback of the perturbation channel.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgps\fB \fR\- the trained model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenabled\fB \fR\- 
 \fB1\fR enables, \fB0\fR disables; a negative value (the default) only reads the current state.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the currently effective flag. When enabled, perturbed genes without outgoing edges
 (all non transcription factors in a TF to target prior) spread their change to the genes
 that share the same upstream regulators.
.PP
